                    </p>
                    <p>The design of a fire network involves a detailed evaluation of the facility to identify risks and determine coverage needs. Hydraulic calculations ensure adequate water supply, pressure, and flow rates, while the pipe layout strategically places hydrants and sprinklers for optimal protection. The design incorporates appropriate fire protection systems based on the facility’s requirements, ensuring compliance with standards like NFPA and BIS. Integrated alarm and detection systems enable prompt activation during emergencies. Rigorous testing verifies system performance, and comprehensive documentation and maintenance guidelines are provided to ensure long-term reliability and safety.</p>
